* Wed Nov 17 2017 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 1.6.0-0BX48
- IPv6 support added. On Gateway changes (IPv4/IPv6) or when otherwise
  triggered, our handlers/constructors check if IPv4, IPv6 or dual stack
  is possible beased on the presence of the respective gateways. 
  Depending on these checks dovecot.conf gets a new listen directive and
  sendmail.mc is extended to bind to IPv4, IPv6 or both. The catch is
  that Sendmail isn't truly dual stack. Best we can do in dual stack is
  to bind it to all IPv4 addresses and the primary IPv6 IP address.
